  <!-- Security and PCI -->
  <section id="security-pci">
    <h2>Security and PCI Compliance</h2>
    <p>
      All e-commerce sites handling payment data must comply with PCI-DSS (Payment Card Industry Data Security
      Standard). Here is how each platform handles it:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">Hosted Platforms (Shopify, BigCommerce, Squarespace, Wix)</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">Full PCI compliance handled by the platform. You do not need to worry
          about security certificates, server configurations, or compliance audits. SSL certificates included.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">Self-Hosted (WooCommerce)</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">You are responsible for PCI compliance. However, using payment gateways
          like Stripe or PayPal (which handle card data externally) significantly reduces your compliance burden to SAQ
          A level - the simplest tier.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

